  <page_number>49</page_number>
  <running_head>LYRICA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>D</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p>
    <l>Vltor ligato fortior agmine,</l>
    <l>Gentísque tandem corda recolligas</l>
    <l>Diuísa, nec posthac redire</l>
    <l>Indigenas patiare motus.</l>
    <l>Nam veris instar vultus vbi tuus</l>
    <l>Plebi nitescet pacificus tua,</l>
    <l>Nubes serenata recedent,</l>
    <l>Præcipites fugient procellæ.</l>
    <l>Te Gallus hostes auspice Barbaros</l>
    <l>Iusto lacesset Marte potentior:</l>
    <l>Tuísque nunc damnis fruentes</l>
    <l>Vexet eques metuendus hasta.</l>
    <l>Impune captis vrbibus impotens</l>
    <l>Bellum Sabaudus mouerit impium</l>
    <l>Multísque quæsitas periclis</l>
    <l>Vsque tuas retinebit arces?</l>
    <l>Impune Gallis seditionibus</l>
    <l>Centaurus audax riserit Allobrox,</l>
    <l>Versámque Francorum superbis</l>
    <l>Contuderit pedibus coronam?</l>
    <l>Impune tectis proditionibus</l>
    <l>Fidens, &amp; auro, cœperit otium</l>
    <l>Turbare Bernatum, &amp; vetustis</l>
    <l>Fœderibus violare Gentes</l>
    <l>Gallis amicas? Tunde superbiam</l>
    <l>Tantósque fastus Principis exteri.</l>
    <l>Quis arma Francorum, tuísque</l>
    <l>Auspiciis sociata, rumpet?</l>
    </p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Verse lines are set in long-s italic type; the text is rendered as printed. Uncertain readings: "Tuísque" and "Versámque" are as printed. The "D" at lower right is a signature mark.</notes>
